{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChPmB9ZznHcPAh8rG1kzB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I routed issue #411 to the engineer, both for the plan and for the code change (status `done`), and wrote `.ard/411/triage-lead.md`.\n\n- **What it is:** `TestBranchesStress` sometimes fails because the main lane's `git fetch` reads a branch lane's worktree folder while that worktree is only half added or removed. `ard serve` runs the same lanes at the same time on one clone, so this could also break close-out commits in production. The request is clear and doesn't touch any of the files agents may not change.\n- **Who plans it:** only the engineer. The only other triage role is lead itself.\n- **Who builds it:** the engineer worker. The change is in Go, mainly the committer and gitx code, and possibly wtlock.\n- **Reviewers:** no `review:` entries were needed. The one reviewer, eng-review, has no `when:` rule in `.ard/config.yaml`, so it reviews every pull request anyway.\n\nI left two notes for maintainers:\n- The plan should first confirm the race can happen in production. The fix should be a lock; retrying the fetch on this one error should only be a backstop.\n- The acceptance criteria ask for 200 repeated runs with the race detector, which is slow. The plan should say whether that runs in CI or only locally."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":620,"cache_read_input_tokens":13350,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":620},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"49ecf8dc-cfc5-4e8b-ace2-fe2fc58a4742","uuid":"1a7a0536-8279-401b-b66d-5d7fc286be64","timestamp":"2026-11-25T13:56:47.799Z","request_id":"req_011ChPm